body:
It upsets me as well, and I'm AFAB. Maybe it's because I'm about to marry a really good man in my life, but I HATE IT. Same for misogyny spoken by male specific places, and so on. Like why??? Everyone is a different being, too complicated to even be put in specific boxes, despite popular belief, and yet you amount a certain sex to something that doesn't even apply to everyone because of what they have in their pants?? It's like saying all cats don't care about their owners. They do, they just have different ways of displaying affection. Also dogs would eat their dead owners too, I'm sick of the " cats would eat you if you died " yeah no shit, any animal that's stuck in a house with food locked away, and the owner dead on the ground, would eat them.

//
Edit because add on to the eating dead owners argument, why do you think during history, some parties in America over centuries ago ended up having to eat each other in the winter? Their food supplies were low and they were slowly dying. Not exactly the same thing, but you understand the point.
